<gpx version="1.1" creator="Flores Race Planner (pipeline/export_gpx.py)" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1 http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1/gpx.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <name>Inerie full circuit via Gurusina and the Sewowoto coast</name>
    <desc>Inerie full circuit via Gurusina and the Sewowoto coast (loop): Round the whole cone: Bena to the rebuilt village of Gurusina, down the wild south flank to the sea at Sewowoto (Ena Bhara beach), then the coast road west to Aimere. Network-routed; the middle leg has the maximum remoteness index and is unscouted. 34.8 km, +421 m. Replaces 29.8 km / +566 m of the main course.</desc>
    <link href="https://github.com/technicaloutdoor/Flores-Race"><text>Flores Race Planner</text></link>
    <time>2026-09-05T06:27:58Z</time>
  </metadata>
  <wpt lat="-8.877400" lon="120.985700">
    <ele>831.0</ele>
    <name>Bena</name>
    <desc>km 0.0 | kind: checkpoint | resupply: minimal | water: unreliable | sleep: homestay -- Ngada megalithic village 19 km south of Bajawa in Tiwuriwu village, Aimere district, at the foot of Inerie; proposed cultural checkpoint, agreement with the village council required before race day.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
    <type>anchor/checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.896240" lon="120.990980">
    <ele>392.8</ele>
    <name>Gurusina</name>
    <desc>km 5.2 | kind: checkpoint | resupply: minimal | water: unreliable | sleep: homestay -- Ngada traditional village on the south-east flank of Inerie, rebuilt after the August 2018 fire; anchor for the Inerie full-circuit option (Bena -&gt; Gurusina -&gt; Sewowoto coast -&gt; Aimere). Position from the Overture gazett</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
    <type>anchor/checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.926340" lon="120.927180">
    <ele>37.9</ele>
    <name>Sewowoto (Ena Bhara beach)</name>
    <desc>km 19.3 | kind: village | resupply: none | water: unreliable | sleep: none | position approximate -- Coastal hamlet and community-tourism beach (Pokdarwis Ena Bhara) at the foot of Inerie's southern slope; the low point of the Inerie full-circuit option before the coast road back to Aimere. Position from the Overture ga</desc>
    <sym>Residence</sym>
    <type>anchor/village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.843000" lon="120.857000">
    <ele>14.4</ele>
    <name>Aimere</name>
    <desc>km 34.8 | kind: port | resupply: basic | water: unreliable | sleep: homestay -- South-coast port of Ngada Regency, ~1 hour south of Bajawa; ASDP ferry to Waingapu (Sumba, Tue/Fri) and Kupang. Exact pier coordinates not found in sources; placed at a low-elevation coastal point inside Ngada near the d</desc>
    <sym>Anchor</sym>
    <type>anchor/port</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.830000" lon="120.851000">
    <ele>46.0</ele>
    <name>Aimere Arak Coast</name>
    <desc>[highlight, position approximate] The south-coast strip around Aimere port, known for small-scale distilling of arak (palm/lontar spirit) alongside its role as the Ngada ferry port to Sumba and Kupang.</desc>
    <sym>Waypoint</sym>
    <type>poi/other</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.877400" lon="120.985700">
    <ele>831.0</ele>
    <name>Bena</name>
    <desc>[anchor] A Ngada megalithic village of nine clans at the foot of Inerie, with paired ngadhu (male) and bhaga (female) ancestor shrines around a stone-terraced central square; among the more visited traditional villages in Ngada.</desc>
    <sym>Museum</sym>
    <type>poi/traditional-village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.896000" lon="120.991000">
    <ele>394.5</ele>
    <name>Gurusina</name>
    <desc>[highlight, position approximate] Ngada megalithic village commonly cited ~21 km from Bajawa; a fire on 13 August 2018 burned 27 of 33 traditional houses and 6 sacred structures, since rebuilt with traditional materials and techniques.</desc>
    <sym>Museum</sym>
    <type>poi/traditional-village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.878000" lon="120.953000">
    <ele>2129.2</ele>
    <name>Inerie</name>
    <desc>[highlight, hike-a-bike] A near-perfect stratovolcano cone (2,245 m) south of Bajawa overlooking the Savu Sea; the highest peak in Ngada and the visual anchor of the megalithic-village section. Not currently active.</desc>
    <sym>Summit</sym>
    <type>poi/volcano</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.869500" lon="120.986000">
    <ele>934.2</ele>
    <name>Luba</name>
    <desc>[highlight, position unverified] A small Ngada megalithic village a few hundred metres from Bena, four clans, ngadhu and bhaga shrines decorated with carved horses, buffalo and snakes; quieter and less visited than its famous neighbour.</desc>
    <sym>Museum</sym>
    <type>poi/traditional-village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.840700" lon="120.961200">
    <ele>1113.0</ele>
    <name>Tololela</name>
    <desc>[highlight, position unverified] A Ngada megalithic village in Manubhara, Jerebuu district, ~30 km from Bajawa on a steep hillside (~650 m); fewer tour groups reach it than Bena.</desc>
    <sym>Museum</sym>
    <type>poi/traditional-village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.835000" lon="120.980500">
    <ele>1537.4</ele>
    <name>Wolobobo Hill</name>
    <desc>[highlight] A sunrise viewpoint hill (~1,700 m) in Turekisa village, ~15 km from Bajawa, with a panoramic view of Inerie volcano and the Bajawa plateau.</desc>
    <sym>Scenic Area</sym>
    <type>poi/viewpoint</type>
  </wpt>
